    m_FontSize: 24
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 1
    m_MaxSize: 300
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "* Credit goes to Alpharad and Kobazco for making the ROM hack \"Pok\xE9mon
    Too Many Types 2\" that specifically adds MissingNo as a regular Pok\xE9mon with
    a more modernized sprite so I don't have to just use the sprite frim the official
    Pok\xE9mon Red and Blue (which looks bad in a GBA/DS art style). Note that the
    front sprite is from said ROM hack (as well as Pok\xE9mon Evolved), but the back
    sprites, icon sprites, and shiny colors are edited.\n* Credit goes to my older
    brother, chase_i_guess (on YouTube and Spotify, and in real life) who introduced
    me to Pok\xE9mon when I was around 12 years old, and also gave me several ideas
    for this game.\n* Credit goes to my high school computers teacher (name withheld)
    for assigning my class a project to make a Pok\xE9mon battle simulator in C++.
    My project ended up just being a stat generator for the Kanto first partners,
    but I did also buy Pok\xE9mon Red to do research, and I grew to really like the
    game, and the whole franchise, in the process. This game is a spiritual successor
    to the stat generator, but it's far more advanced than the one from 12th grade,
    since it's an actual game."
