  m_Text: "* Credit goes to JaidenAnimations (on YouTube) for making videos where
    she did Nuzlocke challenges of Pok\xE9mon Ruby, Platinum, and HeartGold/SoulSilver.
    Those videos inspired me to do Nuzlocke challenges of my own, and also make my
    own Pok\xE9mon content once I got the hang of making animations.\n* Credit goes
    to the guy (name withheld) who hosted these coding classes for Scratch (a programming
    language/website for kids) and taught my class through modules how to code basic
    games and animations in Scratch when I was 13.\n* Credit goes to Nintendo and
    Game Freak for creating Pok\xE9mon in general. Many of the sprites, tiles, and
    audio samples were also made by people working for Nintendo and GameFreak.\n*
    Credit goes to Gnomowladny\r on Pokemon Showdown for the original custom battle
    sprite of Valerie, which I resized from 80x80 to 64x64 and then tweaked so the
    sprite wouldn't look cheaply bitcrushed or something."
